  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "When Is It Safe to Paint After Storm Drywall Repair?",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "HH Remodeling LLC"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
    "url": "http://coloradoremodeling.company"
  },
  "articleBody": "It's totally understandable to want to get your home back to normal after storm damage, and painting is usually the last step. But rushing this can cause more problems! The golden rule is: painting should only happen once the drywall is completely dry, and all moisture issues are fully resolved. Painting over damp drywall is a big no-no because it can lead to stains bleeding through, the paint not sticking properly, or even future damage reappearing. Think about it, if the wall isn't dry, any moisture trapped underneath can cause new issues. Also, if the storm damage involved any contaminants or mold, make sure those adjacent affected materials have been properly cleaned and addressed *before* you even think about applying finish coatings. Skipping these crucial steps often means you’ll be redoing the work later. If you're unsure if everything is ready for paint, it's a good idea to have a professional like HH Remodeling LLC take a look. They can ensure your repaired walls are perfectly prepped for a lasting finish.",
